    "ruleType": "detachment-rule",
    "group": "Penitent Host",
    "summary": "As each battle round starts, you may pick one Vow of Atonement; it applies to your army until the next battle round starts. Each Vow can be picked once per battle.\n\n- **The Path of the Penitent**: your **PENITENT** models get +3\" Move.\n- **Absolution in Battle**: when a unit of yours is picked to fight after making a Charge move earlier this turn, melee weapons of its **PENITENT** models get +1 Attacks and +1 Strength until the phase ends.\n- **Death Before Disgrace**: when a melee attack destroys a **PENITENT** model of yours that is yet to fight this phase, roll a D6; on a 2+ it stays in play, may fight once the attacking unit's attacks are done, then is removed.",
